  "why": "Cast-time spells sit on the d-pad with no trigger: you stop to cast them anyway, so moving your thumb off the stick costs nothing. Instant spells sit on the trigger layers' face buttons, which you can press while moving. Main attacks are on RT, the interrupt is always RT + B and the emergency defensive is always LT + B, so they are the same button on every class. Cooldowns and rare utility are behind LT + RT. Set 2 (LB + RB + d-pad right) holds out-of-combat things: buffs, pets, travel, hearth. The pet's interrupt (Spell Lock or Seduction) is the RT + B macro. Where the spellbook groups a family (forms, aspects, pets, auras, stances) into one flyout, drag the flyout instead to free slots.",
